    <briefdescription>
<para>Specialized shape representing a circle. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class inherits all the functions of <computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1Transformable" kindref="compound">sf::Transformable</ref></computeroutput> (position, rotation, scale, bounds, ...) as well as the functions of <computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1Shape" kindref="compound">sf::Shape</ref></computeroutput> (outline, color, texture, ...).</para>
<para>Usage example: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">sf::CircleShape<sp/>circle;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">circle.<ref refid="classsf_1_1CircleShape_1a21cdf85fc2f201e10222a241af864be0" kindref="member">setRadius</ref>(150);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">circle.<ref refid="classsf_1_1Shape_1a7dbbed35b7544a9e592acd3908713256" kindref="member">setOutlineColor</ref>(<ref refid="classsf_1_1Color_1a1d0a7892f248dc1a8e38e96e4d308109" kindref="member">sf::Color::Red</ref>);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">circle.<ref refid="classsf_1_1Shape_1a5ad336ad74fc1f567fce3b7e44cf87dc" kindref="member">setOutlineThickness</ref>(5);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">circle.<ref refid="classsf_1_1Transformable_1a47c1375b57cbb0e513286e8d11f6dd4d" kindref="member">setPosition</ref>({10,<sp/>20});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">...</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">window.draw(circle);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>Since the graphics card can&apos;t draw perfect circles, we have to fake them with multiple triangles connected to each other. The &quot;points count&quot; property of <computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1CircleShape" kindref="compound">sf::CircleShape</ref></computeroutput> defines how many of these triangles to use, and therefore defines the quality of the circle.</para>
<para>The number of points can also be used for another purpose; with small numbers you can create any regular polygon shape: equilateral triangle, square, pentagon, hexagon, ...</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1Shape" kindref="compound">sf::Shape</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1RectangleShape" kindref="compound">sf::RectangleShape</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1ConvexShape" kindref="compound">sf::ConvexShape</ref></computeroutput> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
